{"name":"Brassy Tint","hex":"#d8ab39","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brassy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Resembling brass.","Impudent; impudently bold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of brassie (“type of golf club”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brassy"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"brassy":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-brassy1.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/32/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-brassy1.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-brassy1.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/32/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-brassy1.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-brassy1.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.or